    "narrative": "The clear anchor for the Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup today is **Brice Turang** (65.44), who secures the top spot due to his high-utility profile against the starter's pace. Given that Stolen Bases are our primary deficit to cover, the combination of a favorable matchup and a projected #2 spot in the order maximizes his opportunities to disrupt the battery. Following him, **Travis Bazzana** (56.66) is an intriguing play; despite the modest base projection, his efficiency is buoyed by a +10% SP skill adjustment and a platoon advantage that pushes him into \"Strong\" territory. Conversely, **Josh Naylor** (54.98) and **Seiya Suzuki** (52.65) remain reliable daily contributors, though both face moderate resistance from their respective opponents, forcing us to lean on their high recency metrics to maintain their standing in the lineup.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal status of **Jose Caballero** (44.61), who barely cleared our threshold for inclusion. While he provides necessary depth, his output is hampered by a significant -14% SP skill penalty and a sub-optimal position at the bottom of the order. He was nearly benched in favor of our deeper bench assets, but with **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Trevor Story** either sidelined by scheduled off-days or IL stints, our flexibility is currently constrained. We are essentially riding our active depth\u2014including **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014to navigate this mid-week stretch.\n\nRisk mitigation remains the primary concern for today\u2019s slate. The lineup for **Brice Turang** is currently pending, and while our projections assume the #2 hole, any shift down the order would immediately prune his efficiency score. Furthermore, we are operating with a cautious eye on game caps; while **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** are active, their scores sit dangerously close to the \"Below floor\" mark of 40. Should early game conditions shift\u2014specifically if wind or weather reports turn unfavorable at the parks hosting **Seiya Suzuki** or **Travis Bazzana**\u2014we are prepared to pull back to preserve our remaining cap availability for the high-leverage weekend series.",
